-- 🎯 a public entry point of the module; 📦 a declaration the translation pulled in.
-- Every term below is a `Term`, so it is terminating by construction.  A recursion is
-- one of the four schemes of `LeanScript.FixSplit` — `fixStructTail`, `fixStructDeep`,
-- `fixWfTail`, `fixWfDeep` — the product of *how it descends* (structurally, on one
-- named argument, in the order the language fixes; or well-foundedly, on the subject
-- Lean's `termination_by` names) by *where the self call stands* (tail: a `while`
-- loop, no frame; deep: native recursion).  No scheme carries a measure the front end
-- had to invent.  A `Tail` scheme's `by decide` is the check that every self call is
-- in tail position; the descent field is Lean's own `decreasing_by` proof, and it is
-- rendered as `sorry` because the front end does not transcribe proof terms yet.
-- What became of the declarations of the module:
--   3 are programs below
-- Nothing is left out.
